{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLGHHZUiAtXtra7uJfEK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added one small piece: `sin(x).rewrite(sinc)` now returns `x*sinc(x)`, which makes the `sinc` case possible. The `sin` case needed no code change, but plain `trigsimp(f)` still doesn't simplify either expression; you have to use `simplify`:\n\n```python\n>>> f = S(1)/2*(-I*exp(I*k) + I*exp(-I*k))\n>>> simplify(f)\nsin(k)\n>>> simplify(f/k).rewrite(sinc)\nsinc(k)\n```\n\n- **`sin(k)`:** `simplify` already gets there. It hands exponentials to `exptrigsimp`, which recognises the pattern once the terms are combined into a single product.\n- **`trigsimp` itself:** it still returns `f` unchanged. Its default method only acts on expressions that already contain trig functions. `exptrigsimp` also fails on this exact input, because it only looks at single products and here the two terms are separate. Fixing that would change how `trigsimp` behaves in general, so I didn't, to keep the fix small.\n- **`sinc(k)`:** this is the change. The 3-line `_eval_rewrite_as_sinc` method is added to `sin` in `sympy/functions/elementary/trigonometric.py`. It is the reverse of the existing `sinc(x).rewrite(sin)`.\n\n**Tests:** in `sympy/functions/elementary/tests/test_trigonometric.py`, 61 pass and 1 fails (`test_sin_cos_with_infinity`). That test fails the same way with my change removed, so it isn't caused by this patch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":318,"cache_read_input_tokens":32279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":318},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aadec93b-65ca-4449-99a0-4123fb5bdbe2","uuid":"d8ab15a3-a90e-408b-acf2-cf1c5a6de52a","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:36:08.497Z","request_id":"req_011ChLGHHR3fwnar6nSUFbBk"}
